What is adapted from it here (issue #417, step 3): the wire of scrcpy 3 as
its protocol note documents it (the stream's start, the packets' header, the
Back and video-reset control messages), its 16-byte SEMU header before each
frame, and how one stream serves several viewers (src/middleware.ts): the
codec's configuration kept and put before every key frame, a viewer that
joins or falls behind waiting for the next key frame while the server is
asked for one. In Go in internal/node/device (scrcpy.go, view.go); the web
client reads the SEMU header (web/src/features/device). The code is
Hypomnema's own.
